-- title:
--   Weierstrass preparation at a smooth special point
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring which is henselian local, is not all of $L$, and satisfies: for all $a,b \in A$ with $a \in \mathfrak m_A$ and $b \neq 0$ there is $n$ with $b \mid a^{n}$. Let $F$ be a field over $L$ which is essentially of finite type and satisfies `IsCurveOver L F` (principal divisors of degree $0$ for every nonzero element, finite residue extensions at all places, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ free of rank one over $F$). Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally finitely presented morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varphi : F \cong X$'s function field a ring isomorphism carrying the image of $A$ in $F$ to `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase`. Let $x \in X$ lie over the closed point of $A$, be closed (every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$) and lie in the smooth locus of `toBase`, and let $\eta \neq x$ lie over the closed point with $x$ a specialisation of $\eta$. Let $Fbar$ be a field over the residue field of $A$ and $R$ a `RegularProlongation A F Fbar`: a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers} \subseteq F$ meeting $L$ exactly in $A$, with a surjective homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ to $Fbar$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \operatorname{Res}(A) \to Fbar$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has an $L$-multiple in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue; assume $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is, as a subring, the image $S_\eta$ in $F$ of the stalk of $X$ at $\eta$. Put $S :=$ the image in $F$ of the stalk at $x$, and assume: the image of $A$ lies in $S$; $Q$ is a place of $Fbar$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring containing the image of that residue field, with principal ideals) which is rational, i.e. its residue field is generated by the residue field of $A$; every $f \in S$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue in $Q$'s valuation ring; for $f \in S$, $f$ is a unit of $S$ if and only if $\operatorname{ord}_Q$ of its $R$-residue is $0$ and that residue is nonzero; and $T \in S$ has $R$-residue of $\operatorname{ord}_Q$ equal to $1$. Then for every $h \in S$ with $h \neq 0$ and $h^{-1} \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ there are a monic $P \in A[U]$ all of whose coefficients below the leading one lie in $\mathfrak m_A$, and $w \in S$, such that $P(T) = h\,w$ in $F$, the coefficients of $P$ being mapped through $A \to L \to F$.
--
--   This is the Weierstrass preparation step at a smooth closed point $x$ of the special fibre of a semistable-type model: any $h \in \mathcal O_{X,x}$ which becomes a unit in the valuation ring attached to the component through $x$ divides, up to a factor in $\mathcal O_{X,x}$, a distinguished polynomial in a coordinate $T$ cutting the reduction of $x$ to order one. It is used in the proof that an element of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ whose $R$-residue lies in every relevant valuation ring already belongs to $\mathcal O_{X,x}$, i.e. in the local description of the model near a smooth special point.
